<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1929" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">allĕvātĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adl-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A raising up</i>, <i>elevating</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">umerorum adlevatio atque contractio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					11, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>an alleviating</i>,
				<i>assuaging</i>, <i>easing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut (doloris) diuturnitatem adlevatio
					consoletur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 1, 12, 40</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nullam adlevationem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Fam.
					9, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
